i thought it was  pretty cowardly kind of pretty bush  league  which  you know there's plenty of tape out  there to watch i haven't seen it replay  but yes i really haven't seen it  anything like that yet  i'm fine i'm good good to go  that's mason rudolph after the game  after he's hit in the head with his own  helmet and fortunately he's fine which  is also very fortunate for miles garrett  because i think the punishment would  have been worse if there would have been  a severe concussion inflicted on a guy  who was knocked out cold last month on a  hit from raven's safety earl thomas  let's hear what mike tomlin the coach of  the steelers had to say after the game  when he was asked about that moment that  happened with only eight seconds left  i'll keep my thoughts to myself you guys  saw what happened at the end  you have no comment about it that's  exactly what i said i got no comment  have you ever seen anything like that at  the end of the game no more questions  regarding that because i'm saying  nothing  here's why mike tomlin said nothing and  also the steelers pr people were doing a  very aggressive job of getting their  guys to zip it quickly so they didn't  say much about what happened now marquis  pouncey had some things to say i mean  some of it was unavoidable there was a  memo that was sent by the league october  11 2019. i got i have a copy of it here  the gist of it was don't criticize  officials and we've seen a couple of  players gets get fined because of it  baker mayfield was fined 12 500 for  public comments criticizing officials  clay matthews had a tweet unrelated to a  game he was even playing in it was the  lions packers game with the trey flowers  illegal use of the hands hands of the  face penalties that got clay matthews  upset he got fined for the tweet at the  bottom of this memo it's clear that  league policy prohibits public criticism  of opponents you cannot make accusations  or criticism of opposing coaches or  players etc and i think the steelers  keenly aware of that so in that moment  they know look these are things that we  can't air out publicly if we've got  issues with what happened we need to  take it up with the league through the  proper channels and i think mike tomlin  to his credit in the moment understood  if i go all in on the browns at this  podium i'm gonna have an issue with the  league office and i think that's why for  the most part the the venom that that we  heard from the steelers was somewhat  muted and add on to that mike mike  tomlin has two guys in this uh situation  that might be facing suspension  themselves and that's mason rudolph and  marquise pouncy so anything he says in  this post-game press conference could  then be shown as him being a hypocrite  if he goes and blasts miles garrett and  says you can't do any of this stuff  after the whistle or after a play well  again miles garrett was the was kind of  the guy who went too far but marquis  pouncey started kicking miles garrett in  the head after the play when they're in  the end zone so i think he did a good  job of making sure he didn't uh say  something that could then be used  against him when talking about his own  players and what they did in the in in  the brawl  and pouncy said after the game that he's  sort of blacked out in the moment and  look  and this gets back to the point you were  making and this doesn't mean i'm  agreeing with your point but there's a  moment where  that that  that command kicks in almost  unconsciously you got to protect your  quarterback you got to protect your  teammate and once somebody crosses the  line as far as miles garrett does we're  in uncharted territory here we don't  know how the other human beings are  going to react in that moment when they  see an opponent remove the helmet of the  quarterback and whack him in the head  with it and i think what marquise  pouncey did big cat is what a lot of us  would do in that situation when we see  it go that far i mean what do you do do  you just you take a step back and say oh  that's an unfortunate development or do  you jump in and try to keep it from from  getting worse and in the process you  become an aggressor and here's what i  can guarantee you today this morning i  guarantee you that the members of the  cleveland browns locker room are  disappointed in miles garrett because  they know he's going to be facing a  suspension for a long time he lost his  cool and he's one of their best players  i guarantee you that the guys in the  steelers locker room love what marquis  pouncey did because he stood up for his  teammate  and in that moment yeah he went too far  too but it does feel a little different  because he was standing up for his  quarterback who just got bashed upside  the head with a helmet  and miles garrett still had his helmet  on at the time i i still  and there's nothing funny about this  stuff but i always chuckle i always  chuckle when someone punches someone in  the head who's wearing a helmet you're  not going to inflict any damage on him  you're only going to inflict damage on  you when you punch a helmet  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

